{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 11, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Most Wondrous Itinerary for a Journey to the Fair Land of Japan**\n\n**Act I: Scene I – The Land of the Rising Sun**\n\nUpon thy arrival in the mighty city of Tokyo where the neon lights doth dance like fairies in the night prepare thyself for a feast of wonders.\n\n**Day One: The Imperial Dominion**\n\nO’er the great gates of the Imperial Palace thou shalt tread with reverence. Let thy steps be light as thou wanderest through the East Gardens where the whispers of history do linger. Then hie thee to the Meiji Shrine to pay homage to the spirits of old where the torii stands tall and the trees do bow in silent prayer.\n\n**Day Two: The Floating World of Edo**\n\nVenture forth to the district of Asakusa where the Senso-ji Temple doth gleam in the morn. Let thy soul be cleansed at the thunder gate. Then wander through the lanes of Nakamise where the merchants cry their wares like minstrels of old. In the evening seek the Kabuki-za Theatre to witness the drama of the past reborn.\n\n**Act II: Scene II – The Ancient Capital of Kyoto**\n\nWith the rising sun thou shalt journey to the city of Kyoto where the temples do whisper tales of emperors and gods. Let thy journey begin at the Kiyomizu-dera where the wooden stage doth jut o’er the city like a promise from the heavens.\n\n**Day Three: Temples and Gardens**\n\nUnto the Fushimi Inari Shrine with its thousand torii gates that wind like serpents up the mountain. There let thy spirit wander and dream. Then to the Arashiyama Forest where the bamboo doth sway and the river doth sing. In the evening visit the Gion district where the geisha do glide like ghosts of beauty past.\n\n**Day Four: The Art of the Samurai**\n\nAt the Kinkaku-ji the Golden Pavilion shall dazzle thine eyes like a jewel set in emerald. Then to the Nijo Castle where the nightingale floors do creak as whispers of intrigue once did. In the twilight seek the Ryoan-ji where the garden of stones doth challenge the mind to find its harmony.\n\n**Act III: Scene III – The Sacred Isle of Miyajima**\n\nTake ship or train to the isle of Miyajima where the torii gate doth stand in the sea as though it were a bridge to the heavens. Let thy heart be stirred by the Itsukushima Shrine where the tides do kiss the sacred stones.\n\n**Day Five: The Isle of the Gods**\n\nAt dawn ascend the Mount Misen where the monkeys do play and the view doth steal thy breath away. In the evening wander the streets of the isle where the deer do bow as though in greeting to royalty.\n\n**Act IV: Scene IV – The Modern Marvels of Osaka**\n\nJourney to the bustling city of Osaka where the laughter of the people doth fill the air like music.\n\n**Day Six: The Castle of the Sun**\n\nBehold the Osaka Castle where the walls do gleam white and the banners do flutter in the breeze. Let thy mind wander through the museum within where the tales of war and peace do live. In the evening seek Dotonbori where the lights do dance upon the waters and the takoyaki doth tempt thy taste buds.\n\n**Day Seven: The Festival of the People**\n\nShould thy stay be prolonged by fate then let it be on the seventh day that thou dost join in the matsuri if the season doth permit. Let thy hands be painted by the artists and thy belly be filled with the delights of the land.\n\n**Epilogue: The Farewell**\n\nWhen the time hath come to depart from this fair land take with thee the memories of the temples the gardens the castles and the people. Let Japan live forever in thy heart as the cherry blossom doth live in the spring. Fare thee well and may the gods of the rising sun smile upon thy journey.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -1.5614248514175415}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.06447542458772659}, {"token": " Most", "logprob": -0.2750755250453949}, {"token": " W", "logprob": -0.3082088232040405}, {"token": "ond", "logprob": -7.271740287251305e-0